Patch-ID: P-APP-001 (slice 1) — host-owned NSApplication singleton and
lifecycle bridge scaffolding.
Rationale: first milestone of engine/docs/patches/P-APP-001.md, reference
approach A (upstream base::RunLoop keeps driving -[NSApp run] on the main
thread; no external pump adapter). Creates the additive rearc_bridge source
set and redirects RegisterBrowserCrApp() to instantiate ReArcApplication (a
BrowserCrApplication subclass), so all upstream pump/class CHECKs pass
unchanged while Cocoa termination entry points route through the engine
lifecycle host. Adds the exported C ABI surface (rearc_engine_entry_mac.h:
ReArcEngineBridgeVersion, ReArcEngineSetLifecycleCallbacks) and the
ReArcAppDelegate scaffolding (installed only by later slices; unreferenced
by upstream hooks in this slice). With no lifecycle host installed, behavior
is stock: terminate falls back to the AppController path and the ReArc
delegate is never installed.
Also in this patch: chrome/browser/ui/webui/version/version_ui.cc shows
"ReArc <version>" on chrome://version (about:version branding; thematically
part of the P-BUILD-001 warm-up, folded in by concurrent authorship — a
documented rule-3 scope deviation).
Build notes from the compile gate:
- rearc_engine_entry_mac.mm stores the opaque host pointer as raw_ptr<void>;
  Chromium's raw_ptr clang plugin rejects raw pointer members (first compile
  attempt failed on this; fixed in-patch).
- The C ABI symbols carry REARC_ENGINE_EXPORT default visibility: Chromium
  compiles with -fvisibility=hidden in every configuration, so without the
  attribute the symbols are not dlsym-able from the framework even in this
  component dev build. chrome/app/framework.exports is updated as well; it
  is only consulted for non-component/non-sanitizer links
  (chrome/BUILD.gn:1365,1418), which remain a later release-packaging gate.
Drift check @ 156.0.8078.74 (2026-11-01): none. All seams from P-APP-001.md
verified in-tree — RegisterBrowserCrApp (chrome_browser_application_mac.mm:39),
BrowserCrApplication +sharedApplication/-terminate:/-cancelTerminate:,
ChromeMainDelegate::PreBrowserMain -> RegisterBrowserCrApp
(chrome_main_delegate.cc:1939), ChromeBrowserMainPartsMac::PreCreateThreads
nil-delegate/AppController/BuildMainMenu block (chrome_browser_main_mac.mm:151),
